Subject: [PATCH] Make /courses level filter and search functional
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Previously the level chips were decorative <span> elements and the
search box had readOnly on the input — neither did anything.

Changes:
- Level chips are now <Link>s that append ?level=X to the URL. Active
  chip is highlighted with the BrenUp purple gradient, inactive ones
  are the standard grey pill. Chips with 0 courses are hidden.
- 'All' chip links back to /courses (or /courses?q=... to preserve
  search) and is highlighted when no level filter is active.
- SearchBox is now a real <form method=GET> that submits ?q= to
  /courses. The input stays populated with the current search value.
  The ⌘K hint is replaced with a ↵ submit button since the box is
  now interactive.
- CoursesPage accepts searchParams and filters allCourses server-side
  by active level (exact match) and search query (title + topic,
  case-insensitive substring).
- filteredCourses drives the course grid so the displayed cards
  actually reflect the active filters.
- Two distinct empty states: 'No published courses yet' (DB empty) vs
  'No courses match your filters' (filters too narrow), the latter
  including a Clear filters link.
- A result summary bar ('Showing X of Y · Level B1 · Search ...')
  with a Clear filters link appears below the chips whenever a filter
  is active.
- Level+search filters compose: picking B1 then searching 'grammar'
  shows only B1 courses whose title or topic contains 'grammar'.
